  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "If \\(\\diamond\\) and \\(\\triangle\\) are whole numbers and \\(\\diamond \\times \\triangle = 36,\\) the largest possible value of \\(\\diamond + \\triangle\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(15\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(37\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Because the product is \\(36\\), neither whole number can be \\(0\\). We can list the positive factor pairs with the smaller number first, since reversing a pair leaves its sum unchanged.\n\nThe smaller factor is at most \\(6\\): if both factors were larger than \\(6\\), their product would exceed \\(36\\). Testing \\(1\\) through \\(6\\), with \\(5\\) giving no whole-number partner, gives every possible pair:\n\\[\n(1,36),\\ (2,18),\\ (3,12),\\ (4,9),\\ (6,6).\n\\]\nTheir sums are respectively\n\\[\n37,\\ 20,\\ 15,\\ 13,\\ 12.\n\\]\nThus every allowed sum is at most \\(37\\), and the pair \\(1,36\\) attains it. The largest possible value is \\(\\boxed{37}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
